        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Five to ten years</strong> maintained, two to three neglected —
            the variable is lubrication, not mileage. Check the belt annually while you have it
            slackened for cleaning, and replace it for a polished centre strip, fraying edges, a
            gritty underside, or slipping that lubrication does not fix.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Any separation of the layers means replace it now rather than plan to. Assess the deck at
            the same time and <a href="/treadmill-maintenance-cost/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">flip it if it is reversible</a>
            — the machine is already apart and it doubles deck life for labour alone.
          </p>
        </div>
